WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.380
An island, drawn as a simple outline.

2
00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.700
On it, a son is born.

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.240
Years later, a newcomer
arrives and takes charge.

4
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:12.000
The island-born son becomes his servant.

5
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:17.560
The son protests: "This island’s mine, by
Sycorax my mother," His mother's island,

6
00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:18.620
he says.

7
00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.970
So who was really there first?

8
00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:24.220
In this mission, you'll meet
post-colonial criticism:

9
00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:28.110
who rules, who is ruled,
and who is made the Other.

10
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.790
You'll read Caliban's claim
closely, in his own words.

11
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.230
And you'll see the age of new
colonies the play was written in,

12
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.260
and how Caribbean
writers later rewrote it.

13
00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:41.280
Your mission: work out
who was there first,

14
00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.240
and what that does to his claim.
